pint.json
# No environment file enters the image, at any depth. A pattern is matched
# against the path relative to the context root, so a bare ".env" excluded this
# directory's file and nothing else — leaving docker/stacks/.env, which holds
# the estate's DB_ROOT_PASSWORD, inside the context for the vendor stage's
# `COPY . .` to pick up. Releases are built by CI from a clean checkout, where
# neither file exists, so no published image carried one; a local `docker build`
# would have. Configuration reaches a container through its environment, never
# through a file baked into a layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*
.phpactor.json
.phpunit.result.cache
/.codex
